{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/pulls/9832","id":4763426071,"node_id":"PR_kwDOLj5faM8AAAABG-wdFw","html_url":"https://github.com/marin-community/marin/pull/9832","diff_url":"https://github.com/marin-community/marin/pull/9832.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/marin-community/marin/pull/9832.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/issues/9832","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/pulls/9832/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/pulls/9832/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/issues/9832/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/statuses/4e533e768d5342e705976bd704cfe63af6b99eed","number":9832,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"[grug] Leave ragged MoE transport rows unwritten when nothing reads them","user":{"login":"mcwitt","id":319411,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxOTQxMQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/319411?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt","html_url":"https://github.com/mcwitt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcwitt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The ragged all-to-all MoE stops zero-filling and overwriting transport rows that no consumer reads, and on GPU builds its dispatch buffer with one scatter. Outputs, drops and gradients are bitwise unchanged. One MoE layer's forward and backward is 4.4-4.8% faster and its compiler temp 1.37 GB smaller, and the hero step shortens by 1.44% (13.737 to 13.542 s). The dispatch scatter, measured together with its backward use in #9833, shortened the step by a further 1.14%.\n\nThe expert chunks write disjoint rows of the dispatch and return buffers, but the custom VJP around `ragged_all_to_all` differentiated each write as an overwrite, so every layer's backward spent a [TK, H] select, add and zero fill on rows the next chunk would ignore. Each written row holds nothing before its one write, and for such a row an overwrite has the derivative of an add, so the transpose passes the output cotangent through unchanged. With every consumer reading only rows a collective wrote, the buffers need no fill: on GPU they come from a Triton kernel that writes nothing, elsewhere they are zero-filled. Each buffer is tied to a loop-carried value, because XLA would otherwise hoist an input-free buffer out of the layer loop and copy it into every layer's output slot. Dropped and padded slots get combine weight 0, and the combine and dispatch-gradient sums skip them. A GPU test fills every buffer with NaN instead of zero and requires identical outputs, drop counts and gradients.\n\nOn GPU, a Triton kernel builds the expert-sorted dispatch buffer by reading each token's row once and writing it to the token's accepted slots, where a gather read every row topk times: 0.535 ms (6.6 TB/s) at the hero's per-GPU routed shape (TK = 524288 rows of the 3072-wide latent). Its weighted form serves #9833's backward. The gather-sum's forward loops over 1024-wide hidden tiles, which keeps more programs resident: 0.508 ms against 0.574 ms.\n\nStep times are single runs on one 64-GPU hero rack (restore step-180000, seed 0, 100 steps) from #9708's measurements.\n\nSplit from #9708. Part of #9636.\n","labels":[{"id":10166074947,"node_id":"LA_kwDOLj5faM8AAAACXfH-Qw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/labels/agent-generated","name":"agent-generated","description":"Created by automation/agent","color":"1D76DB","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":11981276996,"node_id":"LA_kwDOLj5faM8AAAACyiPHRA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/marin-community/marin/labels/agentic-lint","name":"agentic-lint","description":"Local agentic lint review completed","color":"1D76DB","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-06T19:07:27Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T20:08:20Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"00063372742fcca5eef3e69b496fa26b3b8ad0dd","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"dlwh","id":9633,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2MzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9633?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh","html_url":"https://github.com/dlwh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dlwh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"marin-community:mcwitt/ragged-unwritten-transport","ref":"mcwitt/ragged-unwritten-transport","repo":{"id":775839592,"node_id":"R_kgDOLj5faA","name":"marin","full_name":"marin-community/marin","owner":{"login":"marin-co